I commented on the two issues this session's commits touched, closed one, and left the rest alone.

• #1042 — closed. Commit ff1ed5c9 makes /spawn's instruction-file loader check the deny and allow lists that /cd applies, using the same guard as the file tools. It also takes src/context.rs off the list of unguarded readers, so the count drops from 2 to 1. In the comment I said two things plainly:
  • The tests run the loader with local deny and allow lists. Nobody did the end-to-end run on the built binary that the issue suggested as step one.
  • /context's file listing still reads without that check. It only shows file names to the user, and the reader list can't see it.
• #1041 — progress comment, kept open. Commits 4117b0a0 and 0fd1ed52 now connect a server whose tool names clash with a builtin under a prefix (fs__read_file, or mcp1__… for a --mcp server) instead of skipping it. The comment covers how the prefix is chosen and the one-line stderr message. It also notes that the model isn't told those tools are missing, and that the docs now say "prefixed". The live check passed: the filesystem server connected and the model called one of its prefixed tools. It stays open for two reasons:
  • The new connect code starts a fresh client instead of reusing the one from the pre-flight check, so a prefixed server is still started twice.
  • I haven't filed the upstream issue about yoagent offering a prefixed connect.
